## Customer-status taxonomy (EDIT THIS)

> What `prospect / active / churned` mean for your business — specifically
> what makes an account a **current (active) customer**, and what counts as
> **churn**. This is the definition the current-customers list depends on.

- `prospect` — an account we're selling to; no won deal yet. (default)
- `active` — **a current customer** — has at least one won deal and an
  ongoing relationship. (default)
- `churned` — was active, no longer is. (default)

**What makes an account `active` (a current customer):** at least one lead
reached `won` and the relationship is live. (default)

**What counts as churn (`active → churned`):** the customer has ended the
relationship / stopped buying. (default — set your real definition: contract
not renewed? no activity in N months? explicit cancellation?)

